// FoundryGate usage reconciliation (#39 / #84) — billing-grade per-developer token totals.
//
// Run it by hand: Log Analytics workspace > Logs, set the time range to the billing period, paste.
// The Function passes the period as the query's *time range* rather than a literal in the text, so
// this file is parameter-free and the same query answers for any period you select in the portal.
//
// Two tables, because neither alone is enough:
//   ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog   per-request prompt/completion/total tokens and the model, from the
//                                "Logs related to generative AI gateway" diagnostic setting.
//                                It does NOT carry the APIM subscription.
//   ApiManagementGatewayLogs     the gateway's request log, which does carry ApimSubscriptionId.
// CorrelationId is the same value on both rows for one request, so it is the join key.
//
// Caveat (documented in #84 and on the architecture overview): an interrupted stream can leave the
// LLM log with a low or missing token count, so these totals are a floor, not a ceiling. Enforcement
// does not depend on them — the gateway's own token-quota counter is what returns 403.
ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog
| where isnotempty(CorrelationId)
| join kind=inner (
    ApiManagementGatewayLogs
    | where isnotempty(ApimSubscriptionId)
    | project CorrelationId, ApimSubscriptionId
  ) on CorrelationId
| summarize
    PromptTokens = sum(PromptTokens),
    CompletionTokens = sum(CompletionTokens),
    TotalTokens = sum(TotalTokens),
    RequestCount = count()
  by ApimSubscriptionId
| order by TotalTokens desc
